														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863512">
									

<p>Great write-up, but this is just the beginning.</p>
<p>1) The basic problem is that there is no visible SCP involvement. Even if it is just cursory that needs to be allowed for somewhere, be it an inspection by a Foundation agent, temporary control, or some other option. It's even possible for someone close to the CEO to a double-agent and feeding information to The Foundation; given his interest in the occult, it's a good fit.</p>
<p>2) There's far too much mystery here. What happened to him and his followers is of interest, and it needs to be given a reason of some sort. It doesn't matter if they became animals themselves, become a copse, have just decided to create a mystery cult to defend the body from others, or even another force has started eliminated everyone for the body, but their fate needs to be drawn out or at least hinted at.</p>
<p>Again, overall this is great write-up. There are some minor grammatical errors, but otherwise it's a good start!</p>

							</div>

								
					
