														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863505">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> I just listened to TheVolgun’s fantastic audio rendition of SCP-2137 and was very fascinated with the article as a whole.</p>
<p>The article mentions that highly secret details of the Foundation were leaked on YouTube and iTunes and the efforts to cover up the iTunes incident were imperfect.</p>
<p>It stands to reason then, that maybe some sheltered person hiding behind a sophisticated proxy, or something, managed to download and listen to the songs without having his memory erased, or even being noticed by the Foundation.</p>
<p>I feel that a story following this character as he becomes obsessed trying to get to the bottom of the SCP foundation would be an interesting read.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> I believe the protagonist of this tale would perhaps be some kind of techno-master who spends hours delving into the internet for obscure media. Someone who would notice a strange new album from Tupac appearing on Beyoncé’s iTunes page before it got taken down. The type of guy whose basement is filled with GPUs mining Bitcoin.</p>
<p>I think it would also make sense for this character to be as “off grid” as possible while still having internet access. So he hears about these songs, that sound a lot like Tupac, that are supposedly revealing deeply hidden truths about the world and he pounces on it. Buys the album without a second thought, backs up the songs on multiple drives, and devotes endless effort to figuring out what they mean.</p>
<p>This character would then go on a journey trying to access SCP facilities and finding whatever clues he can as a civilian in the SCP universe.</p>
<p>Perhaps the story could also alternate between perspectives as foundation agents realize there’s a civilian who’s onto them.</p>
<p>I think ultimately the tale would end with the protagonist learning much more than any typical civilian would ever hope to. Like witnessing one or more SCPs firsthand, but getting killed in the process.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Most tales I’ve read are from the perspective of either Foundation Agents, someone in a GoI, or an SCP. I don’t know of many from the perspective of civilians. I also think the leaks from SCP-2137 are an event ripe for exploration.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I’m returning to the SCP wiki after a fairly long absence so I’m sure there are things I’ve missed. I originally formatted this post wrong because last time I posted here no such thing existed. So if this idea has been done, or if it’s very similar to another tale, please let me know!</p>

							</div>

								
					
