						<a href="/forum/t-13971284/lonely-voice">Lonely voice</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863492">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Fantasy, and Supernatural</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: Basically, it's a voice that talks to you when you're alone, separate from any other human contact for a time. It starts as your own thoughts, and diverges from your normal train of thought without your notice. Some people are more inclined to hear it, even when around others, but it talks to anyone separate from humanity for an extended period of time.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: It starts with a psych patient being evaluated for possible anomaly, but a suggestion by one of scientist puts forward the idea that an SCP may be attracted to the situation the patient was in&#8212;he had lived alone for many years, secluded. Tests are done putting people in isolation, and many attest to a divergence of thought from their normal thoughts after a time. This is chalked up to normal psychological phenomena, until patterns are seen in the thought patterns: many suggest being drawn away to be separate from humanity, such as going to isolated geographical places, as well as questioning social norms. Several of the test subjects are found to be heading to isolated areas in forests, and atop buildings over following weeks. Basically, the scientists come to the conclusion that the source of the thoughts are voices coming from a variety of non physical beings that dwell in places less inhabited by humans.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: The fact that it's relatable.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: Ehm, as a possible addition to the narrative, these beings are speculated to be aiding it trying to separate humans from each other one by one, as to aid in making an easier invasion of their own species.</p>

							</div>

								
					
