<blockquote>
<p>it causes them to laugh &amp; enjoy the pain of others?</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>This sounds much more interesting than death or disappearing&#8230; like this anomaly reaching into your emotional state and changing the way your empathy works is intriguing. But then&#8230; what do you want to do with that? For example, what is the ultimate point of the story? Where do you want the arc to go? What are the themes you're working with? At the end of the story, where is it you want the reader to be?</em></p>
<p>I don't have much to say about the escape&#8230;</p>
<p>I think you need to think beyond the core anomaly and consider what your narrative is about. What is the overall point you're going for?</p>

